---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"
import { conditions } from "../../data/docs-content"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="conditions">

          <p>
            Where a capability has a catch, here it is. Rather than leaving these in footnotes, every one of them is
            written out in one place.
          </p>
          <dl class="doc-rows">
            {conditions.map(([term, detail]) => (<div><dt>{term}</dt><dd>{detail}</dd></div>))}
          </dl>
          <p class="note">
            The sandbox flag: from 1.99.91, the next release, operating-system confinement is enabled with the
            <code>VECTOR_SHELL_SANDBOX</code> environment variable. Releases before 1.99.91, such as desktop 1.99.8 and npm CLI 1.99.7, do not read that name, so
            setting it there confines nothing. It is opt-in and off by default, uses a seatbelt profile on macOS and bwrap on Linux
            where installed, and has no Windows equivalent — so on Windows Vector reports that it is running
            unconfined instead of implying protection it cannot provide.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
